sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-source-traceability> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 25-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (referee re-score) — Source and data traceability: 35/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Positives: all 72 distinct video IDs cited by the 25 laws resolve to entries in the catalog (checked here); the six v1 DOIs resolve via doi.org; the catalog records channel ID, snapshot date and per-video descriptions. Deductions: the audit YAML carries 6 references for 25 laws attributed to ~25 different speakers, so 19 laws (2-4, 6, 9-11, 13-17, 19, 21-25) have no DOI or URL anywhere in the audit (-15); the bib has 10 entries, 2 without identifier, and 17 laws have no bib entry (-5); Crossref resolution on 2026-10-24 shows `froese2024` pairs the title of Entropy 25(5):748 (2023) with the DOI of Entropy 26(4):288 (2024), `pigozzi2025` cites article 1112 where the DOI resolves to 1027 (propagated into the bib, the math-KG YAML and the docs), the bib's `biswas2023` title 'Fromasikan to Pavlov: Associative Memory and Learning in Gene Regulatory Networks' is not the title of record for 10.3390/ijms24010285, and `chvykov2021` reads 'active matter' for 'active collectives' (-15); Law 7 is attributed as a 'Verbatim Published Theorem' to Froese, but neither Froese abstract mentions optimal stopping and the 1/e law is Lindley (1961) / Gilbert & Mosteller (1966) (-8); Law 17's constants are repository-internal with no pointer to their origin (-4); the catalog SHA-256 (38aab3be...) is quoted in the Substack article but verified by no code, the README still says '6 governing mathematical laws', and the catalog's `mappedMathLaws` is the stale 6-law taxonomy (-6); the two uncited sources that the law titles name ('Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) Bioelectrochemistry', 'Hoel (2026) Patterns 7:101472') carry no DOI in any file (-4); the Finzi 2026 and Shreesha 2025 entries have no persistent identifier (-3). The references block of this audit adds 14 resolvable identifiers and corrects the four defective entries." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/levin_youtube_channel/README.md L1–L5: README: 'paired with the 6 governing mathematical laws formalized in models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py' - stale relative to the 25-law rewrite; claims 'SHA-256-verifiable' but no hash is recorded or checked <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/datasets/levin_youtube_channel/README.md#L1-L5>",
            "datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib L1–L98: 10 entries total; Laws 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25 have no bib entry <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib#L1-L98>",
            "datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib L53–L62: biswas2023 title 'Fromasikan to Pavlov: Associative Memory and Learning in Gene Regulatory Networks' does not match the title of record for 10.3390/ijms24010285 ('Learning in Transcriptional Network Models: Computational Discovery of Pathway-Level Memory and Effective Interventions') <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib#L53-L62>",
            "datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib L86–L98: finzi2026epiplexity and shreesha2025prisoners: @misc entries with no DOI / arXiv id (an OSF URL only for the latter) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib#L86-L98>",
            "docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L64–L64: Law 7 row: 'O1 Verbatim Published Theorem ... Froese (2024) Entropy 26:288'. Unsupported attribution; the 1/e secretary-problem law predates Froese by six decades and is absent from both Froese papers' abstracts <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md#L64-L64>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.yaml L46–L76: v1 references: 6 DOIs (Levin 2019/2022, Chvykov 2021, Bongard 2023, Pigozzi 2025, Froese 2024) for 25 laws <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.yaml#L46-L76>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.yaml L67–L71: pigozzi2025: venue 'Communications Biology 8:1112'; Crossref gives article number 1027 for DOI 10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.yaml#L67-L71>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.yaml L72–L76: froese2024: title 'Irruption Theory: A Novel Conceptualization of the Enactive Account of Motivated Activity' is Entropy 25(5):748 (2023, DOI 10.3390/e25050748); the listed DOI 10.3390/e26040288 resolves to 'Irruption and Absorption: A Black-Box Framework...' (2024). Neither abstract contains an optimal-stopping or 1/e result <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.yaml#L72-L76>",
            "morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml L1–L8: model_spec.inputs lists datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json; the script contains no reference to that file <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml#L1-L8>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-source-traceability-1> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.35"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-source-traceability-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L202–L228" ;
        dct:description "72 distinct video IDs across the 25 laws; all 72 are present in levin_youtube_catalog.json (checked in this audit)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L202-L228> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

